From acf407075812c641411f2291fa68ca553d82b700 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 14:47:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 59/60] nouveau/vk: nvkmd_horizon, advertise Zcull only where a
 context can be bound
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

has_zcull_info was set from the geometry query alone. That query is
cached by nvGpuInit and answers independently of nvGpuGetZcullCtxSize,
so the two can disagree: the ten numbers arrive and the context size is
0. A context size of 0 is exactly what horizon_gpu_channel_create
refuses to bind a Zcull context for — there is no buffer to allocate —
so the pdev could advertise a capability that no channel in the process
is able to be given. Require both.

And an opt-out, NVK_HORIZON_ZCULL=0, which forces has_zcull_info false
without a rebuild. Zcull is the one capability in this backend whose
failure mode is silent: a fragment wrongly rejected looks like geometry
that was never drawn, not like an error. A console therefore needs a way
to take the other path and compare against it in the same run, which is
what t_vk_zcull is built on, and a way to stand the feature down if that
comparison ever comes back wrong. Read with debug_get_bool_option rather
than a cached DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION, so a test may change it
between two instances in one process — the same choice
MESA_VK_WSI_HORIZON_FORCE_COPY made, for the same reason.

The refusal is logged with which of the three reasons it was, because
"Zcull is off" and "Zcull is off because you asked" are different facts
to find in a log.

mesa-nvk-horizon: Phase 4 — extension 6 (Zcull geometry)
Why: nvGpuGetZcullCtxSize and the cached geometry query are two
 independent answers, and NVK reads has_zcull_info as if one implied the
 other; a device where the geometry arrives and the context size is 0
 advertises Zcull that horizon_gpu_channel_create then refuses to bind
 (horizon/channel/channel.c: "Zcull requested but
 nvGpuGetZcullCtxSize() == 0").
Evidence: source, and the patch series applies and builds. mesa/ at
 MESA_COMMIT + the series, `git am` clean, 58 of 58 before this patch.
 NOT run on a console: no hardware has reported ctx_size 0, so this
 closes a state that is reachable by construction rather than one that
 has been observed.
Upstream: no — it is about two Horizon queries and an environment
 variable named for this backend.

Signed-off-by: mesa-nvk-horizon <mesa-nvk-horizon@localhost>
---
 .gitkeep                                      |  0
 .../vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_pdev.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 .gitkeep

diff --git a/.gitkeep b/.gitkeep
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e69de29
diff --git a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_pdev.c b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_pdev.c
index 91fef5e..13dcd92 100644
--- a/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_pdev.c
+++ b/src/nouveau/vulkan/nvkmd/horizon/nvkmd_horizon_pdev.c
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "util/cache_ops.h"
 #include "util/log.h"
 #include "util/macros.h"
+#include "util/u_debug.h"
 #include "util/u_memory.h"
 
 #include "util/u_math.h"
@@ -254,10 +255,29 @@ fill_dev_info(struct nv_device_info *info,
     *
     * A failure leaves has_zcull_info false, which is what NVK checks
     * before touching the struct; nouveau lets this query fail too.
+    *
+    * SO DOES A ctxsw_size OF ZERO, and that is not the same failure.
+    * The geometry query is cached by nvGpuInit and answers independently
+    * of nvGpuGetZcullCtxSize, so the two can disagree: the ten numbers
+    * arrive and the context size is 0.  A context size of 0 is exactly
+    * the case horizon_gpu_channel_create refuses to bind a Zcull context
+    * for -- there is no buffer to allocate -- so advertising Zcull on
+    * such a device would promise something no channel in this process
+    * can be given.  Announce only what a channel can actually be handed.
+    *
+    * NVK_HORIZON_ZCULL=0 forces the same answer without a rebuild.  It
+    * exists because Zcull is the one capability here whose failure mode
+    * is silent -- a fragment wrongly rejected looks like geometry that
+    * was never drawn, not like an error -- so a console needs a way to
+    * take the other path and compare, and t_vk_zcull is built on exactly
+    * that comparison.  Read through debug_get_bool_option rather than a
+    * cached DEBUG_GET_ONCE, so a test may change it between two
+    * instances in one process.
     */
    horizon_gpu_zcull_info zc;
    horizon_gpu_result zres = horizon_gpu_device_get_zcull_info(dev, &zc);
-   if (zres.status == HORIZON_GPU_OK) {
+   const bool zcull_allowed = debug_get_bool_option("NVK_HORIZON_ZCULL", true);
+   if (zres.status == HORIZON_GPU_OK && zc.ctx_size > 0 && zcull_allowed) {
       info->zcull_info = (struct nv_zcull_device_info) {
          .width_align_pixels = zc.width_align_pixels,
          .height_align_pixels = zc.height_align_pixels,
@@ -275,6 +295,11 @@ fill_dev_info(struct nv_device_info *info,
       info->has_zcull_info = true;
    } else {
       info->has_zcull_info = false;
+      mesa_logi("nvkmd_horizon: Zcull is not advertised (%s)",
+                !zcull_allowed        ? "NVK_HORIZON_ZCULL=0" :
+                zres.status != HORIZON_GPU_OK
+                                      ? "the geometry query failed" :
+                                        "the context size is 0");
    }
 }
 
